A similar calibration methodology was proposed in10 and11. However, these methods were designed for systems observing point sources, which can be calibrated by exposing the antenna to previously characterised sources. This is often not possible, for example in sky-averaged experiments where antennas have wide beams and are non steerable. Therefore, new methods are required.Fig. 2
High-level overview of the machine learning-based calibration framework, applied to a 21-cm cosmology experiment. The 21-cm signal obscured by foregrounds12 is received by the radio telescope as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
