Sky-averaged 21-cm cosmologists are attempting to build the world’s most sensitive thermometer to measure the temperature of the early Universe. The redshifted 21-cm line of neutral hydrogen is a faint radio signal that carries the imprint of the first stars and galaxies formed during the Cosmic Dawn and Epoch of Reionisation12. By mapping these signals from redshift z
